### Code Snippets

```
Example
Test two values to find out if 20 is greater than 
18. If the condition is
true
, print some text:
if (20 > 18) {
  System.out.println("20 is greater than 18");
}
Try it Yourself »

---

Example
Use the
if
statement to test variables:
int x = 20;
int y = 18;
if (x > y) {
  System.out.println("x is greater than y");
}
Try it Yourself »

---

Example
Use the
else
statement to specify a block of code to be executed if the condition is
false
.
int time = 20;
if (time < 18) {
  System.out.println("Good day.");
} else {
  System.out.println("Good evening.");
}
// Outputs "Good evening."
Try it Yourself »

---

Example
Use the
else if
statement to specify a new condition if the first condition is
false
.
int time = 22;
if (time < 10) {
  System.out.println("Good morning.");
} else if (time < 20) {
  System.out.println("Good day.");
} else {
  System.out.println("Good evening.");
}
// Outputs "Good evening."
Try it Yourself »
```
